{"title":"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 39","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the coordinates would be a point on the graph of the inverse of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/1511e4807a649a28fb6a20f54da46a9ab61d3f8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^3 - 2x - 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a1ff1524745f7f4cc9d493376e359255d938d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\left(0, -9\\right) \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\left(0, \\sqrt[3]{-9}\\right) \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\left(0, 9\\right) \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\left(0, -\\frac{1}{9}\\right) \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\left(-9, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"630\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_39&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the constant term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a483ee25b066703890405f0127fef9c31572fb81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, we can immediately realise that the coordinates of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercept of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5645b029c709d015b567e8fb109296991f9dbeca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, -9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f24b2d4cd9ccbf87d23a879b966e32808b6277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{-1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"19\" /> and function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a57cebffb904fde6198e688ce71f3eb7f319706.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{-1}(g(x)) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa346f8799ac66e0bee491f33037f94543e5519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(g^{-1}(x)) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f24b2d4cd9ccbf87d23a879b966e32808b6277.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g^{-1}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"19\" /> is the inverse function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59df22b83e1add81bc899e46fe814e67c2eae22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } \\left(-9, 0\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"104\" height=\"32\" /> must be a point on the inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest\">2025 TMTA Algebra II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High_School_Algebra_II_Contest_Problems/Problem_38&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 TMTA High School Algebra II Contest Problems/Problem 38 (page does not exist)\">Problem 38</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_TMTA_High